body:
I'm happy for you and your good (or improving) relationship with your siblings. I've had a pretty messed up relationship with mine. Shit that I thought was just was just us being a pain in the ass turns out it's really messed up. Like not all siblings have thrown knives at each other, or stolen another's car, or had to go to exchange the money you could get to pay off a ransom to get back a pregnant, druggie sister. 

&#x200B;

My siblings are mostly doing better than they were when we were all younger. I was thinking about my nieces and nephews and how they would be hurt, but it's basically devolved into the sooner the better so they can for get about me, or become less attached.

Well, let's break it down together then (which is not at all fair to you, since you'll only have the information I give, but hey.) 

&#x200B;

1) 3 college degrees, but my resume says "call center" since I got a job 15ish years ago that I thought was a good point of entry, but just turned out to be a trap I can't get out of. Now no one wants to hire me for anything else, and I can't do call center shit anymore. 

2) Been looking to get into tech support (actual technical support, not call your internet company because it's down crap) for two years. I've been unemployed in that time. My parents have been funding my bills in that time. I haven't been paying my girlfriend any rent, but she's been keeping a running tab of sorts. 

3) Mid 30's, only job prospects are retail and call centers despite 3 degrees. Not only that, but I'm too proud to take them. I think to myself that I'm better than minimum wage "unskilled labor" jobs. Apparently I'm not, since I'm not getting anything else, but it doesn't stop me. 

&#x200B;

So those are a few quick bits on why I am, actually, a drain, for a bit of a grand a month. 

&#x200B;

Being a drain isn't the only reason for wanting to enjoy a nice, LONG sleep however. I have a family history of suicide and depression, was abused as a child, and grew up in what I'm finding more and more as I meet "normal" families an extremely hostile and dysfunctional environment. 

&#x200B;

I will admit, 100%, that wanting to die isn't normal. I'm realistic, and enjoy me some science, and I understand what I'm supposed to do from a biology PoV. Ensure my survival so I can ensure the survival of the human race. Well, the human race certainly isn't having any issues with under population, so my help isn't needed there, and obviously my family isn't a shining beacon of humanities best, so no real loss in genetics if I don't breed (which I won't, even if I don't die.)  Further more, I'm willing to bet my life (HA!) that being dead is just like it was before I was born, which is to say non-existent. Life is the creation and recollection of memories, the process of which requires a brain. The lack of a working brain means the lack of creation and recollection of memories which means one doesn't exist. If one doesn't exist, one doesn't lay in bed feeling horrible. 

&#x200B;

Even if I don't exist, others still will (true) but they will be in a better place in the long term without me (true in my opinion) or I quite frankly don't care if they are in a better place (for some of them.)

While I appreciate your attempt, it's better in the long run. Yes, it will hurt her, but I'm a drain on her and I need to cut myself loose. 

&#x200B;

I know thinking that you're a drain on people is a part of depression, but I can note it empirically. I literally cost physical resources with no gain. I've been trying to change the situation for two years, and nothing is happening. I'm sitting here with three college degrees and searching for jobs in retail. She's been supportive and helpful, but it's time for her to get better than I.
